**ASSIGNMENT TITLE:** Assignment 3.1
**PROMPT A:** The historical period was the Early Renaissance.The medium is buon fresco painting. Visual characteristics that can be seen are dim lighting and cold colors to show the sad tone, enough space to show people on earth and angels in heaven grieving,emphasis on how different people express grief (anger,crying,silence,etc). It was created by Gitto and commissioned by Enrico Scrovegni for the purpose of attempting to atone for his father’s sins of usury and redeem his family name. The painting also marks a pivotal transition from medieval Byzantine into Renaissance by introducing spatial depth into art to convey raw and intense emotions and a sense of realism.
**PROMPT B:** The historical time period was the High Renaissance. The medium is a buon fresco painting. Visual characteristics that can be seen are lots of depth and linear perspective to show the vast amount of people. Emphasis on the disagreement and debate between the ancient Greek philosophers, Plato and his student Aristotle, about idealism and empiricism. They stand at the center of the painting and use gestures to communicate their beliefs,(pointing up to heaven and down to earth.) Negative space draws our attention to the other people surrounding them showing visual gestures that they are engaged in a discussion or lost in thought. It was created by Raphael and commissioned by Pope Julius ll to decorate the walls of his private library in the Vatican. The painting was created with the historical purpose of creating harmony between classical philosophy and Christian theology. It’s known for its one-point linear perspective creating negative space which draws our attention across its entire painting to see other philosophers discussing the topic or lost in thought.
